# Available Tools & MCP Server Inventory

When researching or debugging, use the right tool for the job. Here are all available tools, their strengths, and when to use each.

---

## Built-in Agent Tools

| Tool | Purpose | Best For |
|------|---------|----------|
| `WebSearch` | Broad web search with AI-summarized results | Quick lookups, current events, library docs overview |
| `WebFetch` | Fetch full page content as markdown | Reading specific URLs found by search |
| `SemanticSearch` | Find code by meaning in the workspace | Exploring codebase structure, finding implementations |
| `Grep` | Exact text/regex search in workspace | Finding specific symbols, strings, patterns |
| `Glob` | Find files by name pattern | Locating specific files or file types |
| `Task` | Launch subagents for parallel work | Heavy parallel exploration, browser automation, best-of-N |

---

## MCP Server: Tavily (`user-tavily`)

**Best for:** High-quality web search with advanced filtering, deep research, site crawling

| Tool | Purpose | Key Params | Best For |
|------|---------|------------|----------|
| `tavily_search` | Web search with advanced options | `query`, `search_depth` (`basic`/`advanced`), `max_results`, `time_range`, `include_domains`, `country` | Targeted searches with domain/time/country filters |
| `tavily_research` | Comprehensive multi-source research | `input` (detailed task description), `model` (`mini`/`pro`/`auto`) | Deep research topics needing synthesis from many sources |
| `tavily_extract` | Extract clean content from URLs | `urls` (array), `extract_depth`, `format` (`markdown`/`text`) | Reading pages Tavily found without another round-trip |
| `tavily_crawl` | Recursive site crawling | `url`, `max_depth`, `max_breadth`, `instructions`, `select_paths` (regex) | Exploring entire doc sites, finding all pages on a topic |
| `tavily_map` | Site structure discovery | `url`, `max_depth`, `select_paths` (regex) | Listing all URLs under a path before selective extraction |

**Tavily vs built-in WebSearch:** Tavily has higher relevance, `advanced` search depth for thorough results, domain/time/country filtering, and research/crawl/extract tools beyond simple search. Prefer Tavily for non-trivial research and for verifying current knowledge against online documentation.

**Accuracy workflow for online documentation:**
1. Use `tavily_search` with vendor/product/library names plus the exact API, feature, or error.
2. Use `tavily_map` when official docs navigation or URLs are unclear.
3. Use `tavily_extract` to read the exact official pages before implementing or answering.
4. Use constrained `tavily_crawl` with `select_paths`, `select_domains`, shallow depth, and small limits to discover related official pages.
5. Use `tavily_research` for synthesis only after primary docs have been found; verify its cited sources with `tavily_extract` when decisions depend on exact contracts.

