## MCP Server: Cursor IDE Browser (`cursor-ide-browser`)

**Best for:** Live browser interaction — navigating pages, filling forms, taking screenshots, testing UI

Defined in system prompt (no separate descriptor files). Key tools:

| Tool | Purpose | Best For |
|------|---------|----------|
| `browser_navigate` | Navigate to URL | Opening pages |
| `browser_snapshot` | Get page structure as YAML + refs | Understanding page state before interaction |
| `browser_click` | Click element by ref | Interacting with buttons, links |
| `browser_type` | Type text into element | Filling form fields |
| `browser_fill` | Fill/replace input content | Form completion |
| `browser_take_screenshot` | Visual page capture | Visual verification |
| `browser_search` | Search for text on page | Finding content without scrolling |
| `browser_scroll` | Scroll page/container | Reaching offscreen elements |
| `browser_console_messages` | Read browser console | Debugging JS errors |
| `browser_network_requests` | Inspect network activity | Debugging API calls |
| `browser_lock`/`unlock` | Lock/unlock browser tab | Prevent concurrent access |

**Use for:** Frontend testing, verifying UI changes, debugging webapp behavior live.

